## Interface: 11509, 20506, 16001
## Title: Spoken Zones Audio
## Notes: Narrated zone lore for Spoken Zones. Install alongside Spoken Zones.|n|cffffcc00Beta:|r a proof-of-concept voice, being redesigned and re-generated.
## Version: 0.3.3
## Author: rusty
## IconTexture: Interface\AddOns\ZoneLoreAudio\Textures\AddonIcon.tga
## X-License: Audio generated with ElevenLabs from warcraft.wiki.gg lore text (CC BY-SA 4.0).
## X-Credits: Lore text sourced from warcraft.wiki.gg contributors (CC BY-SA 4.0).

# The tier this folder is. scripts/package-audio.sh rewrites these two lines, and
# the Title above, once per tier it builds; the tree in the repository is the
# 128kbps master every shipped tier is transcoded from, so it describes itself as
# the high tier. Data/Sounds.lua reads these back at load time and reports them
# to ZoneLore, which is how two tiers installed side by side can be told apart.
## X-ZoneLore-Quality: high
## X-ZoneLore-Bitrate: 128

# The language this pack narrates, read back the same way. ZoneLore plays only
# packs matching the language it is showing text in: an English voice reading
# under German prose is worse than the silence it would replace.
## X-ZoneLore-Language: enUS

# Defines the ZoneLoreAudioPacks registry entry that ZoneLore reads. No dependency
# is declared in either direction: ZoneLore reads its lore without narrating when
# no pack is present, and a pack is inert without it.
Data/Sounds.lua
